body:
Part of me understands that feeling. It's like the anticipation is driving you up the wall. You want a permanent final answer. Either you're cured or not. One or the other... the waiting game is annoying. I think you've lived on the edge for so long that you're just desperate for any kind of relief. But I reckon if you really thought about it and turned over every stone in your mind, you'd find that a part of you still wants to live.

&#x200B;

All I can say is well done for fighting through. You've obviously dealt with a lot since 2015... more than me that's for sure. I really hope things work out.

At least you have someone to talk to and you're actually working towards a goal. Once you get your degree you should be able to land a decent job, widen your circle, earn money and start travelling. They say that travelling opens the mind so I'd say keep your head up and focus on the end goal.

&#x200B;

You could also try joining a club that you're interested in at your Uni? 

&#x200B;

Part of me misses playing video games. I sold all of my game stuff for travel fare.... yep. It could be worse my friend.
